%n akul | aklam | enkīdu | [simat (|) ilūti]
#note: See @bib{RN117@316}: “a obv. 14-15. The closest parallel to this couplet is not OB II or SB II but SB VII 136-7: @i{ša ušākilūka akla simat ilūti / kurunna išqûka simat šarrūti} (cf. also SB VI 27-8).”
// cf. L I.4 OB "II" 96-97
// cf. L I.4 SB "II" 50
// cf. L I.4 SB "VII" 136

%n [kurunna | šiti | sim]at (|) šarrūtim
// cf. L I.4 OB "II" 98
// cf. L I.4 SB "II" 51
// cf. L I.4 SB "VII" 137

%n gilgāmeš | umm[aka | ulidka? | ...]
// cf. L I.4 OB "II" 234-235
// cf. L I.4 OB "Harmal₂" 42

%n [ša šumšu | ittana]mbalu | qaqqa[ru]
#note: See @bib{RN117@316}: “d 2'. Though the Yale tablet has @i{ittanambalā mātātum}, this version certainly had something different, of masculine gender, and ki = @i{qaqqaru} seems the obvious candidate..”
// cf. L I.4 OB "III" 183

%n [qabal (|) lā mahā]r || šubat | huw[āwa]
// L I.4 OB "III" 115-116
// L I.4 OB "III" 200

%n [... | tušakši]daššu | ana mahrīya
#note: See @bib{RN117@316}: “a rev. 1'. Ḫuwawa is speaking to Enkidu: cf. SB V 91: [@i{ammēni lemn}]@i{iš Gilgāmeš tušakšidu adi maḫrīya}.”
// cf. L I.4 SB "V" 121

%n [... | ē tāhu]z | aššata | u lalêša
#note: See @bib{RN117@316}: “a rev. 3'. Ḫuwawa curses Enkidu; cf. the fragmentary SB V 253-7, especially @i{lal}[@i{ê} in l. 254.”
// cf. L I.4 SB "V" 277

%n [... | irt]appudā | ina ṣēr (|) muhhīšu
#note: See @bib{RN117@316}: “a rev. 5'. Wilhelm supposed that the subject of [@i{irt}]@i{appudā} is the winds that Šamaš sent to blind Ḫuwawa. It might instead be Ḫuwawa’s auras, whose frantic efforts to escape are described with this verb in OB Ishchali 17': @i{kīma watmū irtanappudū iq-qīšim}.”
// cf. L I.4 OB "Ishchali" 17'

%n [... tū]r | arah | nēršū-ma
#note: See @bib{RN117@317}: “Restored after OB Ishchali 18': @i{šâtu tūr nērma}.”
// cf. L I.4 OB "Ishchali" 18'
